.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt IOREG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ioreg
.Nd show the I/O Kit registry
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ailrx
.Op Fl c Ar class
.Op Fl d Ar depth
.Op Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl p Ar plane
.Op Fl w Ar width
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the I/O Kit registry as a tree: each object's name and location,
then its class, registry id, busy count (in the IOService plane) and
retain count.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Print the registry as an XML property list instead: each object's
properties, with
.Ql IORegistryEntryName ,
.Ql IOObjectClass
and its children in
.Ql IORegistryEntryChildren .
.It Fl c Ar class
Only objects of
.Ar class ,
or of a class derived from it.
.It Fl d Ar depth
Only that many levels.
.It Fl i
Show each object's class inheritance.
.It Fl k Ar key
Only objects with the property
.Ar key
(and, with
.Fl l ,
only that property).
.It Fl l
Show the objects' properties.
.It Fl n Ar name
Only objects named
.Ar name
(or
.Ar name Ns @ Ns Ar location ) .
.It Fl p Ar plane
The registry plane to show: IOService (the default), IODeviceTree,
IOPower, IOACPIPlane...
.It Fl r
With
.Fl c ,
.Fl k
or
.Fl n ,
the subtrees under the objects found too.
.It Fl w Ar width
Cut lines to
.Ar width
characters; 0 does not cut them.
The terminal's width by default, or no limit when the output is not a
terminal.
.It Fl x
Numbers in hexadecimal.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
1 when
.Fl c ,
.Fl k
or
.Fl n
found nothing; 0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvram 8 ,
.Xr system_profiler 8
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
